## Framework 5: OPA/Rego Policies

Use for plan-time governance evaluated against `terraform show -json` output.

### Policy Convention
- Package per area: `{{COMPANY_SLUG}}.naming`, `{{COMPANY_SLUG}}.tags`, `{{COMPANY_SLUG}}.network`
- Expose violations as a **set named `violations`**
- Test files: `{policy}_test.rego` co-located with policy file

### Policy Template

```rego
package {{COMPANY_SLUG}}.{{POLICY_AREA}}

import rego.v1

violations contains msg if {
    some resource in input.resource_changes
    resource.type == "{{TERRAFORM_RESOURCE_TYPE}}"
    resource.change.actions[_] in {"create", "update"}
    {{VIOLATION_CONDITION}}
    msg := sprintf("{{ERROR_MESSAGE_TEMPLATE}}", [{{MSG_ARGS}}])
}
```

### Running
```bash
opa eval --input tfplan.json --data policies/ --fail-defined \
  "data.{{COMPANY_SLUG}}.{{POLICY_AREA}}.violations"
```
